<section id="faq" class="ns-section ns-faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="ns-container ns-editorial-grid">
    <header class="ns-section-heading">
      <p class="sn-eyebrow"><span class="sn-eyebrow__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>Questions</p>
      <h2 id="faq-title" class="t-heading">Before you write</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="ns-faq__items">
      <details>
        <summary>Do you work with the systems we already have?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Email, spreadsheets, a CRM, accounting software, a custom app, Zapier, Make, n8n. I don't ask you to move the business onto a new platform first.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How do we know AI belongs in this workflow?</summary>
        <p>Pick and the Signal Audit exist to answer that. If a checklist, a zap, or a person is the better fix, I will say so. I don't sell a chat window with nothing behind it.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Who owns the work when it is done?</summary>
        <p>You do, once the final invoice is paid: the configuration, prompts, code, and notes produced for you. The model vendor's terms still apply to their service. I don't keep a right to your documents.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What happens after the project?</summary>
        <p>You can stop. Handoff notes are part of the project. If you want it watched, Desk Hours is $2,500 a month after a rollout, Flow Care is $1,500 a month after a Wire, and Managed AI Ops starts at $6,500 a month after a build.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do you take healthcare or patient data?</summary>
        <p>No. I don't take projects whose core data is protected health information, and I don't sign a BAA. The pharmacy figure on this site is from my employment at United Networks of America. Agent Eva was a document workflow. Neither is an offer to handle patient records. Don't put patient information in the contact form.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Who will we actually meet?</summary>
        <p>Me. I scope it, build it, and show up to the readout. I don't staff a bench behind the site.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How quickly do you reply?</summary>
        <p>By email within two business days. The form does not reserve a time on a calendar.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What does the first piece of work cost?</summary>
        <p>Adopt starts at $3,500. Pick is $3,500 and Rollout is $8,500. Automate starts at $7,500. Build starts at $18,000. A Signal Audit, if you need the map before a build, is $4,500.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
